/*!
\page page_stmtdpidtraits StMtdPidTraits

\brief Muon Telescope Detector (MTD) particle identification traits for a matched track.

\section stmtdpidtraits_overview Overview

\ref StMtdPidTraits stores PID information for a track matched to a hit in the STAR Muon
Telescope Detector (|η| < 0.8, r ≈ 400 cm, outside the STAR iron absorber).  The MTD
is the primary tool for muon identification in STAR: hits behind ~5 interaction lengths
of iron strongly suppress hadronic backgrounds.  TOF information provides supplementary
muon/hadron separation.

\section stmtdpidtraits_hierarchy Class Hierarchy

\code{.txt}
StObject
  └── StTrackPidTraits
           └── StMtdPidTraits
\endcode

\section stmtdpidtraits_members Key Data Members

| Member | Type | Description |
|---|---|---|
| \c mMatchFlag | \c UChar_t | Matching quality flag. |
| \c mYLocal / \c mZLocal | \c Float_t | Local track coordinates at the MTD module (cm). |
| \c mDeltaY / \c mDeltaZ | \c Float_t | Track–hit residuals (cm). |
| \c mThetaLocal | \c Float_t | Local incident angle (rad). |
| \c mTimeOfFlight | \c Float_t | Measured TOF (ns). |
| \c mExpTimeOfFlight | \c Float_t | Expected TOF for muon hypothesis (ns). |
| \c mPathLength | \c Float_t | Path length from vertex (cm). |
| \c mBeta | \c Float_t | β = v/c. |
| \c mSigmaMuon | \c Float_t | nσ from the muon hypothesis. |
| \c mProbMuon | \c Float_t | Muon PID probability (0–1). |

\section stmtdpidtraits_example Usage Example

\code{.cpp}
const StMtdPidTraits* mtd = nullptr;
for (const StTrackPidTraits* p : track->pidTraits()) {
    mtd = dynamic_cast<const StMtdPidTraits*>(p);
    if (mtd) break;
}

if (mtd && mtd->matchFlag() > 0) {
    double dtof     = mtd->timeOfFlight() - mtd->expTimeOfFlight();
    double nSigMuon = mtd->sigmaMuon();

    if (std::abs(nSigMuon) < 3. &&
        std::abs(mtd->deltaY()) < 30. &&
        std::abs(mtd->deltaZ()) < 30.) { /* muon candidate */ }
}
\endcode

\see StTrackPidTraits
\see StMtdCollection
\see StTrack
*/
